      "text": "To determine the total number of games played in the baseball league, we can use the following approach:\n\n1. **Calculate the number of unique pairings of teams:**\n\n   Each game involves two teams. Since there are 9 teams, the number of ways to choose 2 teams out of 9 to play a game is given by the combination formula:\n\n   \\[\n   \\binom{9}{2} = \\frac{9!}{2!(9-2)!} = \\frac{9!}{2! \\cdot 7!} = \\frac{9 \\times 8 \\times 7!}{2 \\times 1 \\times 7!} = \\frac{9 \\times 8}{2 \\times 1} = 36\n   \\]\n\n   So, there are 36 unique pairings of teams that can play a game.\n\n2. **Calculate the total number of games played:**\n\n   Each game is played between two teams, so each game contributes 1 to the total count of games. Since there are 36 unique pairings and each pairing results in one game, the total number of games played is:\n\n   \\[\n   36\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the total number of games played in the baseball league is \\(\\boxed{36}\\).",
