      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To determine the total number of games played in the baseball league, we can use the concept of combinations. Specifically, we need to find the number of ways to choose 2 teams out of 9 to play a game, since each game involves 2 teams.\n\nThe number of ways to choose 2 teams out of 9 is given by the combination formula:\n\n\\[\n\\binom{9}{2} = \\frac{9!}{2!(9-2)!} = \\frac{9!}{2! \\cdot 7!}\n\\]\n\nSimplifying the factorials, we get:\n\n\\[\n\\binom{9}{2} = \\frac{9 \\times 8 \\times 7!}{2 \\times 1 \\times 7!} = \\frac{9 \\times 8}{2 \\times 1} = \\frac{72}{2} = 36\n\\]\n\nSo, there are 36 different pairs of teams that can play a game. Since each pair of teams plays 3 games, the total number of games played is:\n\n\\[\n36 \\times 3 = 108\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the total number of games played in the season is \\(\\boxed{108}\\).",
