      "text": "To determine the total number of games played in the baseball league, we start by calculating the number of unique pairings of teams. Since there are 9 teams, the number of ways to choose 2 teams from 9 is given by the combination formula \\( \\binom{n}{k} = \\frac{n!}{k!(n-k)!} \\), where \\( n \\) is the total number of teams, \\( k \\) is the number of teams to choose, and \\( ! \\) denotes factorial.\n\nHere, \\( n = 9 \\) and \\( k = 2 \\):\n\\[\n\\binom{9}{2} = \\frac{9!}{2!(9-2)!} = \\frac{9!}{2! \\cdot 7!} = \\frac{9 \\times 8 \\times 7!}{2 \\times 1 \\times 7!} = \\frac{9 \\times 8}{2 \\times 1} = 36\n\\]\nSo, there are 36 unique pairings of teams.\n\nNext, each pair of teams plays exactly 3 games. Therefore, the total number of games played is the number of unique pairings multiplied by the number of games each pair plays:\n\\[\n36 \\times 3 = 108\n\\]\nThus, the total number of games played in the league is \\(\\boxed{108}\\).",
